Checking customer messages at night has become a persistent habit, one that disrupts sleep patterns and leaves users feeling exhausted. The trigger for this behavior is often a non-urgent order notification, which can be enough to pull them into the dashboard and keep them awake past midnight. This pattern suggests a struggle with setting boundaries between work and personal life, as well as a reliance on technology to manage stress.

In an effort to establish some control, users have experimented with different strategies. One approach has been to give urgent customers a separate ringtone, allowing for more focused attention when needed while still enabling ordinary alerts to be muted. This solution acknowledges the importance of responding to genuine emergencies without sacrificing sleep or daily routines.
